From 21328abaf08e92a9ea5da607195945622c735e05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pedro Harada <pedroyujiharada@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:34:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Fix build and runtime failures on ROS 2 Humble + Gazebo
 Classic

The package did not build, and once building, the simulation started with
no robot in it. Seven independent defects, three blocking the build and
four only visible at runtime.

Build:
- CMakeLists.txt: install(DIRECTORY ...) listed log/ and src/, which do not
  exist in the package, aborting CMake.
- package.xml: <depend>rviz</depend> is the ROS 1 package name; rosdep
  cannot resolve it on ROS 2. Use rviz2.
- package.xml: <depend>libgazebo_ros</depend> exists neither as a ROS
  package nor as a rosdep key. Use gazebo_ros.

Runtime:
- ackermann_with_sensor.xacro: the file included ackermann.xacro, which
  only DEFINES the limo_ackermann macro, but never instantiated it. The
  generated URDF contained the sensors and their joints parented to a
  base_link that was never created, so robot_state_publisher aborted with
  "Failed to build tree" and nothing ever published /robot_description.
  spawn_entity then waited forever on "Waiting for entity xml".
- ackermann.xacro: the base_footprint link and base_joint were commented
  out, while the Gazebo plugin (robot_base_frame) and gazebo.rviz (Fixed
  Frame) both reference that frame. tf2 ended up with two unconnected
  trees and RViz rendered nothing.
- ackermann_gazebo.launch.py: world_path was passed to ackermann.launch.py,
  which ignores it; the include that actually starts Gazebo received no
  arguments, so the world file was dead code.
- worlds/empty_world.model: referenced by the launch file but missing from
  the repository. Added, with a closed room and obstacles so the lidar has
  something to detect.

Usability:
- sensor.xacro: set an explicit frame_name on the lidar plugin. Without it
  Gazebo lumps laser_link into base_link (fixed joint) and /scan is
  published with the wrong frame_id.
- rviz/gazebo.rviz: add a RobotModel display; the upstream config has no
  display that draws the robot.
- .gitignore: the "*.mod*" rule swallows worlds/*.model, which is most
  likely why empty_world.model never reached the repository.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0184gfpVifSX9zuaLAdJhmXh
